<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan to abolish import duty on sugar.</title>
<headline>Pakistan to abolish import duty on sugar.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistani government has decided to abolish a 10 percent import duty on sugar to guard against any shortages, the state television said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It quoted a government spokesman as saying a formal announcement on the matter would be made after a meeting of the Economic Coordination Committee of the cabinet due to be held on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The decision follows a statement by former prime minister Benazir Bhutto expressing fears that Pakistan might soon face shortage of sugar and cooking oil after recent scarcities of wheat that sparked riots in parts of the country.</p>
</text>
